# `print(0)` writes a single `0`. The integer arm peels digits with `/` and `%`,
# a loop that a zero argument never enters, so without the explicit zero digit
# the call would write an empty slice. Printing 0, then 42, then 0 again pins
# both the new arm and the ordinary path either side of it.
print(0)
print(" ")
print(42)
print(" ")
print(0)
exit(0)
